1
00:00:01,835 --> 00:00:03,270
EPISODE 14

2
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:07,207
Sounds like you really
liked Yun-hui back then.

3
00:00:08,375 --> 00:00:09,943
I was basically a stalker.

4
00:00:10,744 --> 00:00:13,614
I followed her around
like a puppy every day.

5
00:00:15,983 --> 00:00:18,585
Do you still have feelings for her?

6
00:00:19,753 --> 00:00:21,688
It's not like that.

7
00:00:24,057 --> 00:00:27,995
But honestly, it does bother me a bit.

8
00:00:29,062 --> 00:00:31,532
Seeing someone I once liked

9
00:00:31,598 --> 00:00:34,001
struggle so much like this,

10
00:00:34,735 --> 00:00:36,937
I feel bad for her,

11
00:00:37,838 --> 00:00:39,873
and it makes me uneasy.

12
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:44,077
I told her that wasn't it, though.

13
00:00:44,945 --> 00:00:46,713
Maybe it's sympathy?

14
00:00:47,447 --> 00:00:49,950
A kind of pity?

15
00:00:50,017 --> 00:00:52,085
Something like that?

16
00:00:52,152 --> 00:00:53,620
I don't think that's it.

17
00:00:53,687 --> 00:00:56,189
Come on, I told you it's not!

18
00:00:56,256 --> 00:00:59,760
I really have no feelings
for her at all, for your information.

19
00:00:59,826 --> 00:01:01,495
That's all that matters, then.

20
00:01:02,763 --> 00:01:05,465
Wow, there are so many stars.

21
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:08,635
-Right?
-Yes.

22
00:01:34,127 --> 00:01:37,698
Let's just go for a walk
since the weather's so nice.

23
00:01:37,764 --> 00:01:41,535
A walk? Sure, a walk sounds great.

24
00:01:48,008 --> 00:01:49,810
Yu-na, try some of this.

25
00:01:49,876 --> 00:01:51,078
Have this.

26
00:01:51,144 --> 00:01:53,547
And… this, and this too.

27
00:01:53,614 --> 00:01:55,382
Eat all of this.

28
00:01:56,483 --> 00:01:57,684
Eat anchovies too.

29
00:01:57,751 --> 00:01:59,953
Okay, I'll eat on my own.

30
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:01,588
Eat up, eat up!

31
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:12,633
Ow!

32
00:02:18,271 --> 00:02:19,706
Honey, what's wrong?

33
00:02:19,773 --> 00:02:22,209
Honey, what's gotten into you again?

34
00:02:22,275 --> 00:02:24,811
Honey! Honey!

35
00:02:26,146 --> 00:02:28,715
What's with them this morning?

36
00:02:28,782 --> 00:02:32,319
So, are we practicing today
for the Paldo Gangsan Singing Contest?

37
00:02:32,386 --> 00:02:34,021
Yes, of course we should.

38
00:02:34,955 --> 00:02:37,024
Why the long face? Is something wrong?

39
00:02:37,090 --> 00:02:39,926
No, nothing. I'm just a bit tired.

40
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:41,628
Eat plenty, everyone.

41
00:02:46,566 --> 00:02:48,535
Now what's wrong with her?

42
00:02:48,602 --> 00:02:50,937
She eats like a horse, yet left food.

43
00:02:53,774 --> 00:02:55,409
Who's calling at this hour?

44
00:02:57,477 --> 00:02:58,712
Darn it.

45
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:01,281
Quiet, be quiet.

46
00:03:03,917 --> 00:03:05,485
Oh, hi, Mom!

47
00:03:05,552 --> 00:03:07,721
I've been good. Have you been well?

48
00:03:08,488 --> 00:03:11,191
Of course, I was studying.

49
00:03:11,258 --> 00:03:12,526
Yes, okay.

50
00:03:13,527 --> 00:03:15,996
Uh… tomorrow? Why? For my birthday?

51
00:03:16,063 --> 00:03:18,498
Mom, state exam students
don't get birthdays.

52
00:03:18,565 --> 00:03:20,667
I have to study.

53
00:03:21,234 --> 00:03:22,869
Get some rest, Mom.

54
00:03:22,936 --> 00:03:25,405
Coming, Teach! Mom, I have to hang up.

55
00:03:27,741 --> 00:03:29,309
"Teacher"? Give me a break.

56
00:03:29,376 --> 00:03:32,846
Wait, your family still thinks
you're studying for the state exam?

57
00:03:32,913 --> 00:03:36,183
Of course. If my mom knew,
I never could've come down here.

58
00:03:36,249 --> 00:03:37,918
If she knew I'm growing cabbage,

59
00:03:37,984 --> 00:03:39,453
I'd get beaten to death.

60
00:03:39,519 --> 00:03:41,588
Wait, is tomorrow your birthday?

61
00:03:43,557 --> 00:03:45,325
Geez, I meant to let it pass.

62
00:03:45,392 --> 00:03:48,128
Now I'm busted thanks to Mom. Gosh.

63
00:03:48,195 --> 00:03:51,264
Everyone's busy, so please
don't fuss over my birthday.

64
00:03:51,331 --> 00:03:53,600
-Really, don't make a fuss.
-Okay.

65
00:03:54,935 --> 00:03:56,737
Got it. Eat up and let's go work.

66
00:03:56,803 --> 00:03:58,438
We have to go catch snails.

67
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:02,142
-Tomorrow's my birthday--
-Oh, Min-gi!

68
00:04:02,209 --> 00:04:04,277
I'll go help you work today too.

69
00:04:04,344 --> 00:04:07,981
You too? No, the work's way too hard.

70
00:04:08,048 --> 00:04:09,583
What if you get recognized?

71
00:04:09,649 --> 00:04:11,518
I'm just so cooped up. Please?

72
00:04:13,019 --> 00:04:14,721
You really shouldn't.

73
00:04:18,825 --> 00:04:21,962
-It'll be bad if the locals find out.
-Got it.

74
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:25,999
-Hello.
-Hey there.

75
00:04:26,066 --> 00:04:27,434
-Hello.
-Field work, y'all?

76
00:04:27,501 --> 00:04:28,969
But who's she? A new face.

77
00:04:29,035 --> 00:04:30,604
Her name's Yu-na, they say.

78
00:04:30,670 --> 00:04:33,473
What? Yu-na?

79
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:42,916
I'm Sang-deuk. Nice to meet you.

80
00:04:42,983 --> 00:04:44,217
Wow.

81
00:04:54,261 --> 00:04:56,196
Why does my body feel like this?

82
00:05:07,274 --> 00:05:08,942
It's eleven o'clock.

83
00:05:10,110 --> 00:05:13,747
Hey, get up! Hurry and wake up!

84
00:05:13,814 --> 00:05:17,250
Let me sleep a little longer.

85
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:21,655
I'm dead tired from digging all night.

86
00:05:21,721 --> 00:05:24,624
We have to go out and paint.

87
00:05:24,691 --> 00:05:26,126
Hurry and get up.

88
00:05:26,193 --> 00:05:28,929
That stupid mural.

89
00:05:28,995 --> 00:05:32,032
We could just pretend to paint.

90
00:05:32,098 --> 00:05:34,267
Why are you working so hard at it?

91
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:36,703
It's the only way to avoid suspicion.

92
00:05:37,804 --> 00:05:40,273
If you hate it, pack up and head back.

93
00:05:46,713 --> 00:05:50,851
Hey, why do you look so pale?

94
00:05:50,917 --> 00:05:52,452
Are you feeling sick?

95
00:05:52,519 --> 00:05:56,256
No, I'm just feeling a little off.

96
00:05:58,558 --> 00:06:01,962
Hey, quit lazing in bed and come eat!

97
00:06:02,028 --> 00:06:04,931
Yes, we'll be right out.

98
00:06:08,101 --> 00:06:10,403
You're still sprawled out this late?

99
00:06:10,470 --> 00:06:13,240
I swear, you two are lazy to the bone.

100
00:06:20,313 --> 00:06:22,816
Did you set the table yourself, sir?

101
00:06:22,883 --> 00:06:26,219
Yes, my daughter-in-law
said she was going to church,

102
00:06:26,286 --> 00:06:28,488
so I set the table myself.

103
00:06:28,555 --> 00:06:30,790
Not many side dishes, but eat plenty.

104
00:06:30,857 --> 00:06:32,325
Thank you for the food.

105
00:06:41,368 --> 00:06:43,904
These days, I… actually

106
00:06:43,970 --> 00:06:45,939
really prefer plain rice.

107
00:06:46,907 --> 00:06:48,708
Me too, me too!

108
00:07:01,321 --> 00:07:03,757
What on earth is with that old man?

109
00:07:03,823 --> 00:07:07,894
Why does he keep trying to feed us
things he was sucking on himself?

110
00:07:07,961 --> 00:07:12,299
And Sang-deuk or Man-deuk,
why is that jerk so feisty?

111
00:07:12,365 --> 00:07:15,135
What, is he a feisty rural guy,
an FRG or something?

112
00:07:15,201 --> 00:07:18,104
Didn't I say no one in town is normal?

113
00:07:18,171 --> 00:07:20,607
Not a single one is normal. Not normal.

114
00:07:20,674 --> 00:07:22,208
Su-yeon!

115
00:07:24,744 --> 00:07:26,880
Here comes that nutjob again.

116
00:07:32,485 --> 00:07:33,954
Hello, yes.

117
00:07:34,921 --> 00:07:36,923
Han-cheol, what brings you by again…

118
00:07:36,990 --> 00:07:39,092
I brought you some cabbage to try.

119
00:07:39,159 --> 00:07:41,795
We grew this cabbage ourselves.

120
00:07:41,861 --> 00:07:45,098
It tastes simply amazing, just amazing!

121
00:07:45,165 --> 00:07:47,701
See all these big holes right here?

122
00:07:47,767 --> 00:07:50,270
Snails nibbled on them, so don't worry.

123
00:07:50,937 --> 00:07:54,774
-It's heavy, very heavy.
-Okay, thank you. I'll enjoy it.

124
00:07:54,841 --> 00:07:56,843
But Su-yeon, why do you look so weak?

125
00:07:56,910 --> 00:07:58,378
Are you feeling sick?

126
00:07:58,445 --> 00:08:01,014
No, I'm fine.

127
00:08:08,355 --> 00:08:11,224
-Oh my, Su-yeon! What's wrong?
-Su-yeon! Su-yeon!

128
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:31,911
Stop, stop!

129
00:08:31,978 --> 00:08:34,414
How do you get worse
the more you practice?

130
00:08:34,481 --> 00:08:37,317
True, Hwa-ran keeps up pretty well now,

131
00:08:37,384 --> 00:08:38,918
but you're totally shaky.

132
00:08:38,985 --> 00:08:42,555
With this much practice,
even grade-schoolers could do it.

133
00:08:42,622 --> 00:08:44,391
Why do you keep messing up?

134
00:08:44,457 --> 00:08:47,327
I'm sorry. Let's stop now.

135
00:08:47,394 --> 00:08:49,696
What's wrong? Are you sulking again?

136
00:08:50,697 --> 00:08:53,733
No, I really just can't do this.

137
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:57,237
I'll handle the Paldo Gangsan
Singing Contest. Let's stop here.

138
00:08:57,904 --> 00:09:00,774
Yu-na, you worked so hard. I'm sorry.

139
00:09:03,610 --> 00:09:05,045
Yun-hui.

140
00:09:06,846 --> 00:09:08,181
Yun-hui!

141
00:09:16,923 --> 00:09:18,925
Yun-hui, where are you going?

142
00:09:18,992 --> 00:09:20,460
I have to go to work now.

143
00:09:20,527 --> 00:09:23,096
Then let's go together. I'll help you.

144
00:09:25,532 --> 00:09:28,635
I'm not in the mood for your jokes now.

145
00:09:28,701 --> 00:09:30,437
I'm sorry.

146
00:09:42,949 --> 00:09:46,219
It's drizzling. What a dreary day.

147
00:09:46,286 --> 00:09:48,855
Where is Man-gu,
and what's he doing all day?

148
00:09:48,922 --> 00:09:51,758
We have a mountain of potatoes to pack.

149
00:09:53,159 --> 00:09:55,095
What's that sound?

150
00:10:20,420 --> 00:10:22,455
Mom, what is it?

151
00:10:24,157 --> 00:10:26,025
Oh, Mrs. Kim, you're here.

152
00:10:26,092 --> 00:10:29,629
Mom! Why are you in such a daze?

153
00:10:29,696 --> 00:10:32,065
Oh… No, it's nothing.

154
00:10:32,132 --> 00:10:34,100
What are you doing here?

155
00:10:34,167 --> 00:10:37,103
You don't need to know. Go on, hurry.

156
00:10:37,170 --> 00:10:39,305
One more time, In-ki. Cue!

157
00:10:39,372 --> 00:10:40,840
Sure, got it.

158
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:53,953
Why do I keep acting like this?

159
00:10:54,020 --> 00:10:56,689
I lose my head whenever I see Mr. Han.

160
00:10:58,458 --> 00:11:02,195
His voice is pure honey,
and he's great on the guitar.

161
00:11:02,262 --> 00:11:04,164
I see him in a whole new light.

162
00:11:06,232 --> 00:11:08,635
What am I even thinking right now?

163
00:11:08,701 --> 00:11:12,305
Sun-bun, Sun-bun.
Snap out of it and get to work.

164
00:11:12,372 --> 00:11:14,474
Oh, I'm still a woman after all.

165
00:11:14,541 --> 00:11:16,176
Oh, dear.

166
00:11:18,545 --> 00:11:20,413
I'm completely out of tape again.

167
00:11:43,069 --> 00:11:45,071
Mrs. Kim, are you all right?

168
00:11:45,138 --> 00:11:47,941
Oh, yes… I'm all right.

169
00:11:48,007 --> 00:11:51,611
You must be careful.
That was a close call, Mrs. Kim.

170
00:11:52,545 --> 00:11:55,114
Well then, I will be on my way.

171
00:12:03,656 --> 00:12:05,592
He is so dashing.

172
00:12:11,331 --> 00:12:13,633
You silly girl.

173
00:12:13,700 --> 00:12:15,235
Speak up when you're sick.

174
00:12:15,301 --> 00:12:17,403
Why hold out until you collapse?

175
00:12:19,205 --> 00:12:20,740
Listen.

176
00:12:20,807 --> 00:12:24,911
The health center doctor
said that it's just a cold.

177
00:12:24,978 --> 00:12:26,713
You should get going now.

178
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:29,482
No, ma'am.

179
00:12:29,549 --> 00:12:33,419
I will stay by Su-yeon's side
and nurse her until she gets better.

180
00:12:33,486 --> 00:12:36,422
I will go get some fresh water, then.

181
00:12:44,197 --> 00:12:45,665
Good grief.

182
00:12:45,732 --> 00:12:48,101
He's a clinger, a real clinger.

183
00:12:49,602 --> 00:12:51,638
Why isn't she coming yet?

184
00:12:52,405 --> 00:12:54,407
I'll stand guard right here

185
00:12:54,474 --> 00:12:56,943
and grab her
to clear up the misunderstanding.

186
00:12:57,010 --> 00:12:58,478
I have to pee.

187
00:12:58,544 --> 00:13:00,113
Nope.

188
00:13:00,713 --> 00:13:02,448
I have to pee while I can.

189
00:13:03,016 --> 00:13:04,684
Am I too far out front?

190
00:13:11,457 --> 00:13:12,792
Sang-deuk.

191
00:13:13,660 --> 00:13:15,061
Mi-yeong!

192
00:13:16,329 --> 00:13:18,364
Why right now, of all times…

193
00:13:18,431 --> 00:13:22,335
Wait, wait! I need to talk to you.

194
00:13:22,402 --> 00:13:25,038
I have nothing to say. Just leave.

195
00:13:26,239 --> 00:13:29,075
Mi-yeong! Just wait a second!

196
00:13:29,142 --> 00:13:31,711
Damn it, I'm going nuts!
Just stop flowing, stop!

197
00:13:31,778 --> 00:13:33,646
Oh, Mi-yeong!

198
00:13:39,752 --> 00:13:40,953
Clear it up, my ass.

199
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:44,190
Why does she only show up
right when I'm peeing?

200
00:13:44,891 --> 00:13:46,693
I'm losing my mind, seriously.

201
00:13:50,196 --> 00:13:53,132
Oh, right.
I should check the township email.

202
00:13:53,199 --> 00:13:55,468
Oh, my goodness. Oh, my.

203
00:13:57,136 --> 00:14:01,507
Goodness, where is my head these days?

204
00:14:05,578 --> 00:14:06,679
Let's see…

205
00:14:09,869 --> 00:14:11,951
WORLD-CLASS PIANIST
LEE HYEON-SEOK ARRIVES!

206
00:14:28,601 --> 00:14:31,971
Min-ho, watch your head!
Watch your head!

207
00:14:32,038 --> 00:14:33,673
Watch your head!

208
00:14:33,740 --> 00:14:37,643
Mom, Min-gi gave me a shoulder ride
all the way here from school!

209
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:39,345
Oh, did he?

210
00:14:39,412 --> 00:14:41,381
He must've been heavy, though.

211
00:14:41,447 --> 00:14:43,516
Get down now. We're here, we're here.

212
00:14:44,150 --> 00:14:45,852
There you go.

213
00:14:46,552 --> 00:14:48,321
You're crazy heavy for your size.

214
00:14:48,388 --> 00:14:50,690
What do you weigh?
My neck almost snapped!

215
00:14:50,757 --> 00:14:52,725
Give me another ride next time, okay?

216
00:14:52,792 --> 00:14:54,494
All right, kiddo.

217
00:14:55,561 --> 00:14:57,964
Are you really not going to practice?

218
00:14:58,030 --> 00:14:59,766
What about the Singing Contest?

219
00:14:59,832 --> 00:15:02,602
I'll handle that, so don't you worry.

220
00:15:02,668 --> 00:15:05,171
What's with you again?
Is something wrong?

221
00:15:05,238 --> 00:15:07,006
It's nothing.

222
00:15:07,073 --> 00:15:09,542
You two, wash up and get ready to eat.

223
00:15:12,578 --> 00:15:16,349
I swear, your mom's hiding something.

224
00:15:21,654 --> 00:15:23,289
Min-ho, was today fun?

225
00:15:23,356 --> 00:15:26,926
Yes, thanks to Min-gi,
I made friends with Wang-bae.

226
00:15:26,993 --> 00:15:28,594
We played after school today.

227
00:15:28,661 --> 00:15:30,897
Oh, good for you!

228
00:15:32,999 --> 00:15:35,935
Oh, right! You had art class today.

229
00:15:36,002 --> 00:15:38,404
Let's see what you drew, Min-ho.

230
00:15:38,471 --> 00:15:39,705
HAPPY FAMILY

231
00:15:39,772 --> 00:15:42,208
My goodness, you drew this so well!

232
00:15:43,309 --> 00:15:45,211
But what did you draw here?

233
00:15:45,278 --> 00:15:48,881
Today's art topic was "Our Family."

234
00:15:50,983 --> 00:15:53,319
Oh, my, you did such a great job.

235
00:15:54,053 --> 00:15:57,356
But who's this? Your great-uncle?

236
00:15:57,423 --> 00:15:59,158
No, it's Min-gi.

237
00:15:59,725 --> 00:16:01,360
-Min-gi?
-Yes.

238
00:16:01,427 --> 00:16:04,630
I think if I had a dad,
he'd be just like Min-gi.

239
00:16:05,998 --> 00:16:07,733
What?

240
00:16:08,367 --> 00:16:12,271
Mom, I'm sleeping with Min-gi tonight.

241
00:16:12,338 --> 00:16:14,440
Mom, see you tomorrow.

242
00:16:26,953 --> 00:16:29,422
HAPPY FAMILY

243
00:16:49,575 --> 00:16:51,644
Oh, you scared me!

244
00:16:54,313 --> 00:16:57,183
It's almost 12 already.

245
00:16:59,185 --> 00:17:00,553
Excuse me.

246
00:17:00,620 --> 00:17:03,556
How long will you stay like that?

247
00:17:04,557 --> 00:17:05,791
Aren't you leaving?

248
00:17:06,759 --> 00:17:09,996
Su-yeon's fever will not go down.
I should stay by her side.

249
00:17:10,062 --> 00:17:12,331
Please don't mind me and go to sleep.

250
00:17:12,398 --> 00:17:16,435
How can I not mind with you like that?

251
00:17:17,169 --> 00:17:18,771
I'm a sensitive person,

252
00:17:18,838 --> 00:17:22,675
so I just can't sleep if you do that.

253
00:17:24,010 --> 00:17:26,579
Gosh, what devotion.

254
00:17:26,646 --> 00:17:28,614
Such devotion.

255
00:17:29,682 --> 00:17:31,717
I really am sensitive, though.

256
00:17:33,486 --> 00:17:36,088
So much for sleep. No sleep for me.

257
00:17:36,155 --> 00:17:38,090
What am I supposed to do…

258
00:17:47,333 --> 00:17:49,001
Ta-da!

259
00:17:50,603 --> 00:17:51,737
Um, honey.

260
00:17:51,804 --> 00:17:55,675
Could I maybe ask what this is?

261
00:17:56,342 --> 00:17:59,512
This? It's seaweed chocolate fondue.

262
00:17:59,579 --> 00:18:02,949
What? Seaweed chocolate what, what-do?

263
00:18:03,015 --> 00:18:05,384
Seaweed chocolate fondue. Fondue.

264
00:18:05,451 --> 00:18:07,887
Today is Ki-jun's birthday, you know.

265
00:18:07,954 --> 00:18:09,822
So I meant to make seaweed soup,

266
00:18:09,889 --> 00:18:11,791
but plain seaweed soup is cliché.

267
00:18:11,857 --> 00:18:15,394
So I put my culinary skills to work.

268
00:18:15,461 --> 00:18:18,531
Then how do we even swallow this?

269
00:18:18,598 --> 00:18:20,199
Could I ask that too?

270
00:18:20,266 --> 00:18:22,134
Oh, you're so uncultured.

271
00:18:22,201 --> 00:18:25,104
Take this seaweed gently like this…

272
00:18:25,671 --> 00:18:28,007
roll it up round and round,

273
00:18:28,074 --> 00:18:31,544
and dip it in the chocolate like this.

274
00:18:31,611 --> 00:18:32,778
Looks tasty, right?

275
00:18:32,845 --> 00:18:34,313
Honey, say "ah."

276
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:36,115
Ah.

277
00:18:36,182 --> 00:18:38,684
What are you doing? She said say "ah."

278
00:18:38,751 --> 00:18:41,253
-Why me?
-Today's your birthday, isn't it?

279
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:44,023
You should eat the most. Am I right?

280
00:18:44,090 --> 00:18:46,058
-That's right!
-Eat up.

281
00:18:46,592 --> 00:18:48,194
-Ah.
-Ah!

282
00:18:52,999 --> 00:18:55,167
Aw, look at you eating so well.

283
00:18:55,234 --> 00:18:56,736
Is it delicious?

284
00:19:00,172 --> 00:19:02,508
-It's pretty good.
-Quit lying.

285
00:19:02,575 --> 00:19:05,711
It's kind of savory and sweet.

286
00:19:05,778 --> 00:19:07,480
This is actually good. Wow!

287
00:19:07,546 --> 00:19:08,914
No way, that can't be.

288
00:19:08,981 --> 00:19:10,750
I mean it. It's good, try some.

289
00:19:10,816 --> 00:19:11,751
-Really?
-Yes.

290
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:12,785
Let Yu-na go first.

291
00:19:12,852 --> 00:19:14,954
-Here, try this.
-Let Yu-na go first.

292
00:19:15,021 --> 00:19:16,422
-What? Why?
-Ladies first.

293
00:19:16,489 --> 00:19:17,590
Here, say "ah."

294
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:22,461
How is it?

295
00:19:25,031 --> 00:19:26,932
Wait, it's actually delicious!

296
00:19:26,999 --> 00:19:28,734
Oh my, what a relief.

297
00:19:28,801 --> 00:19:32,204
I was really torn
between gummy jelly and chocolate.

298
00:19:32,271 --> 00:19:34,507
-What a relief.
-What a huge relief.

299
00:19:35,574 --> 00:19:38,611
I have no appetite. Please excuse me.

300
00:19:42,481 --> 00:19:44,050
What's with her again?

301
00:19:44,116 --> 00:19:45,084
Hold on.

302
00:19:45,151 --> 00:19:48,921
That guy Han-cheol isn't here, though.

303
00:19:48,988 --> 00:19:53,025
Su-yeon's sick, so Han-cheol nursed her
all night and couldn't come home.

304
00:19:53,092 --> 00:19:56,228
Wow, that guy looks like a criminal,

305
00:19:56,295 --> 00:19:58,898
but he's a hopeless romantic, isn't he?

306
00:20:06,305 --> 00:20:09,308
Thank goodness, her fever's way down.

307
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:13,412
Ow, gosh.

308
00:20:22,021 --> 00:20:24,724
Why is this room so messy?

309
00:20:38,170 --> 00:20:39,405
The Clink?

310
00:20:40,172 --> 00:20:42,408
Wow, she has great taste in comics.

311
00:20:43,275 --> 00:20:44,744
What's this?

312
00:20:48,447 --> 00:20:51,751
Is this a map? It looks like a map.

313
00:20:52,618 --> 00:20:53,519
SOUL-MYEON

314
00:20:54,687 --> 00:20:57,823
Uh… What are you doing right now?

315
00:20:58,758 --> 00:21:02,928
The room was so messy,
so I was trying to tidy up for you.

316
00:21:05,397 --> 00:21:08,100
And I found this map here.

317
00:21:08,167 --> 00:21:11,337
What are these red X marks here?

318
00:21:12,171 --> 00:21:13,773
It looks like a local map.

319
00:21:15,074 --> 00:21:16,876
Wait, hold on.

320
00:21:16,942 --> 00:21:18,577
No way!

321
00:21:21,247 --> 00:21:24,884
You marked the sweet potato fields!

322
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:28,487
And the X marks are the fields
you already dug up, right?

323
00:21:29,755 --> 00:21:32,324
That's it, that's right!

324
00:21:33,292 --> 00:21:36,929
Wow, you're really systematic
about raiding sweet potatoes.

325
00:21:36,996 --> 00:21:39,398
You could compete in the Olympics!

326
00:21:39,465 --> 00:21:41,667
Raiding sweet potatoes so passionately,

327
00:21:41,734 --> 00:21:43,602
she was bound to collapse.

328
00:21:45,471 --> 00:21:47,239
I'll put this away for you.

329
00:21:52,278 --> 00:21:54,413
Huh? What's this?

330
00:21:56,081 --> 00:21:59,785
These are outfit samples
for raiding sweet potatoes.

331
00:22:00,586 --> 00:22:02,555
It's nothing like that.

332
00:22:02,621 --> 00:22:04,690
Su-yeon designed those.

333
00:22:04,757 --> 00:22:06,592
-Su-yeon did?
-Yes.

334
00:22:06,659 --> 00:22:10,763
Her dream is to become a designer
and launch her own brand.

335
00:22:11,630 --> 00:22:15,401
But with her college background,
she doesn't stand a chance in Korea.

336
00:22:15,467 --> 00:22:18,804
So people mocked her:
"A no-name college grad trying hard."

337
00:22:18,871 --> 00:22:21,974
"She doesn't know her place."
She was humiliated so much.

338
00:22:22,041 --> 00:22:24,410
She had a really hard time.

339
00:22:29,315 --> 00:22:30,950
I see.

340
00:22:53,873 --> 00:22:56,442
Mi-yeong, why do you look so down?

341
00:22:57,309 --> 00:23:00,179
-I'm fine, don't mind me. Just work.
-Oh, Mi-yeong.

342
00:23:00,246 --> 00:23:02,615
We're out of toilet paper.
I'll go buy some.

343
00:23:02,681 --> 00:23:04,016
Okay.

344
00:23:25,070 --> 00:23:28,107
Sang-deuk, what are you doing here?

345
00:23:32,077 --> 00:23:33,712
Mi-yeong, talk to me.

346
00:23:33,779 --> 00:23:35,581
Talk about what?

347
00:23:35,648 --> 00:23:38,150
I told you we should rethink us.

348
00:23:38,217 --> 00:23:40,386
Rethink? What's there to rethink?

349
00:23:40,452 --> 00:23:42,254
There's no need to rethink it.

350
00:23:42,321 --> 00:23:44,223
I just wasn't ready back then.

351
00:23:44,290 --> 00:23:47,760
But I swear I'm completely ready now.

352
00:23:47,826 --> 00:23:49,962
-Don't do this.
-I told you, didn't I?

353
00:23:50,696 --> 00:23:52,831
I'd never let go of this hand again.

354
00:23:52,898 --> 00:23:55,868
No matter what, I'll never let you go.

355
00:23:55,935 --> 00:23:59,238
What are you doing?
What if someone sees us?

356
00:23:59,305 --> 00:24:01,006
I don't care who sees us.

357
00:24:01,073 --> 00:24:04,510
Until you take back what you said
about rethinking us today,

358
00:24:04,576 --> 00:24:06,445
I'm never letting go of this hand.

359
00:24:17,089 --> 00:24:20,359
Gosh, Mi-yeong, get me some coffee.
I'm dying of thirst.

360
00:24:20,426 --> 00:24:23,228
Yes, just a moment, please.

361
00:24:31,170 --> 00:24:33,939
Jeez, this is driving me crazy.

362
00:24:34,006 --> 00:24:37,409
Why did Sun-bun have to show up then?

363
00:24:37,476 --> 00:24:41,080
Still, why did you hide, you moron?

364
00:24:41,146 --> 00:24:43,882
I've got pointlessly good reflexes.

365
00:24:46,819 --> 00:24:48,187
Oh my, Sang-deuk!

366
00:24:48,253 --> 00:24:50,389
Oh my, oh my!

367
00:24:50,456 --> 00:24:52,091
It's been a while.

368
00:24:52,157 --> 00:24:55,127
Have you been doing well?

369
00:24:56,228 --> 00:24:57,563
Bong-ryeon.

370
00:24:57,629 --> 00:24:59,932
Why haven't you called me?

371
00:24:59,999 --> 00:25:02,034
Oh, you're playing hard to get?

372
00:25:02,101 --> 00:25:04,336
You're acting like a bad boy.

373
00:25:05,604 --> 00:25:07,206
It's nothing like that.

374
00:25:07,272 --> 00:25:09,508
Um, I'm actually busy right now.

375
00:25:12,611 --> 00:25:15,214
Sang-deuk, what brings you here?

376
00:25:15,280 --> 00:25:19,585
-Mom.
-Oh my, Mother! How have you been?

377
00:25:20,319 --> 00:25:22,221
What, are you two dating again?

378
00:25:22,287 --> 00:25:24,123
No, we just met by coincidence.

379
00:25:24,189 --> 00:25:28,260
A date disguised as a coincidence,
shall we say? Something like that.

380
00:25:28,327 --> 00:25:29,962
What are you talking about?

381
00:25:30,029 --> 00:25:32,898
I see. Have you eaten, Bong-ryeon?

382
00:25:32,965 --> 00:25:36,201
If not, since we've met,
why not come eat at our house?

383
00:25:36,268 --> 00:25:39,138
Oh my, should I do that, Mother?

384
00:25:39,204 --> 00:25:40,739
-We're not going!
-Be quiet!

385
00:25:40,806 --> 00:25:43,308
What do you like to eat, Bong-ryeon?

386
00:25:43,375 --> 00:25:46,578
Anything's fine, but my favorite is…

387
00:25:46,645 --> 00:25:48,213
prime ribeye?

388
00:25:56,789 --> 00:26:00,926
Is something up with Yun-hui lately?
She's been in such a bad mood.

389
00:26:00,993 --> 00:26:03,062
Did I do something wrong?

390
00:26:03,128 --> 00:26:05,831
You didn't do anything wrong.

391
00:26:06,465 --> 00:26:08,333
What's up? Why is she like that?

392
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:10,536
I think I know, but I won't tell you.

393
00:26:10,602 --> 00:26:12,805
-Why?
-Just because I'm annoyed.

394
00:26:12,871 --> 00:26:15,007
What do you mean? Why are you annoyed?

395
00:26:15,074 --> 00:26:17,142
Hold on, wait a sec, guys.

396
00:26:17,209 --> 00:26:19,678
Didn't you forget
something way more important?

397
00:26:19,745 --> 00:26:20,979
Forget something?

398
00:26:21,046 --> 00:26:23,015
-No, we didn't.
-What day is today?

399
00:26:23,082 --> 00:26:25,617
-Your birthday.
-So you do know after all!

400
00:26:25,684 --> 00:26:27,386
Then shouldn't you have a gift

401
00:26:27,453 --> 00:26:28,887
or have something to say?

402
00:26:28,954 --> 00:26:31,423
Hey, I even ate that
seaweed chocolate fondue

403
00:26:31,490 --> 00:26:33,158
with you. What more do you want?

404
00:26:33,225 --> 00:26:35,294
Forget it. Not once in eight years

405
00:26:35,360 --> 00:26:38,697
have you celebrated my birthday.
What was I even expecting?

406
00:26:38,764 --> 00:26:40,032
You guys are so petty.

407
00:26:42,835 --> 00:26:44,536
-Hello.

408
00:26:44,603 --> 00:26:46,338
Heading off to work?

409
00:26:49,108 --> 00:26:50,876
Take this.

410
00:26:51,844 --> 00:26:54,746
-What is that?
-I heard it's your birthday today.

411
00:26:54,813 --> 00:26:56,281
I worked hard to get this.

412
00:26:56,348 --> 00:26:57,749
-Really?
-That's right.

413
00:26:57,816 --> 00:27:00,652
Thank you so much, sir. Wow, this is…

414
00:27:03,055 --> 00:27:04,323
what is this?

415
00:27:04,389 --> 00:27:06,125
Deer antler, kid. Deer antler!

416
00:27:06,191 --> 00:27:08,360
It's freshly cut, so it's still warm.

417
00:27:08,427 --> 00:27:10,362
This stuff is unbeatable for men.

418
00:27:10,429 --> 00:27:14,633
I took this last year
and couldn't sleep for all 12 months.

419
00:27:14,700 --> 00:27:16,301
I was bursting with energy.

420
00:27:16,869 --> 00:27:19,471
I get that, and I'm grateful.

421
00:27:19,538 --> 00:27:21,807
You have to slice or brew it
for me to take.

422
00:27:21,874 --> 00:27:23,642
Eat it raw? It's not a dog chew.

423
00:27:23,709 --> 00:27:26,345
Complaining over a gift?
Give it back, kid!

424
00:27:26,411 --> 00:27:28,113
No, no! I'll eat it somehow.

425
00:27:28,180 --> 00:27:30,449
-Thank you so much.
-Sure thing.

426
00:27:30,516 --> 00:27:33,318
-You're the best, sir.
-Ki-jun's pretty wife is here.

427
00:27:33,385 --> 00:27:35,420
-Hi.
-Hwa-ran, what brings you here?

428
00:27:35,487 --> 00:27:37,923
Um, Ki-jun, do you have some time now?

429
00:27:37,990 --> 00:27:40,659
Now? I'm on my way to work, though.

430
00:27:40,726 --> 00:27:43,162
Forget it. We'll do the work for you.

431
00:27:43,228 --> 00:27:45,564
We didn't get you a gift,
so take today off.

432
00:27:45,631 --> 00:27:48,100
Go on, have fun on your date.

433
00:27:48,167 --> 00:27:50,435
Hwa-ran, have a great time.

434
00:27:50,502 --> 00:27:51,570
Let's go.

435
00:27:51,637 --> 00:27:53,238
I said it's not like that!

436
00:27:54,106 --> 00:27:56,074
Thank you for the deer antler, sir.

437
00:27:56,141 --> 00:27:57,643
Follow me.

438
00:27:57,709 --> 00:27:59,311
Where are we going?

439
00:28:08,820 --> 00:28:12,624
Paldo Gangsan Singing Contest prelims
are tomorrow, right? Going well?

440
00:28:12,691 --> 00:28:14,993
Yes, it's going well enough.

441
00:28:15,060 --> 00:28:18,931
You really need to pass the prelims
and make the finals this time.

442
00:28:18,997 --> 00:28:21,667
That way, we can promote
our Indi County apples

443
00:28:21,733 --> 00:28:24,069
and sell the apples piled in storage.

444
00:28:24,136 --> 00:28:27,172
Don't worry. I'll do my very best.

445
00:28:27,239 --> 00:28:30,075
All right, I'm counting on you.

446
00:28:30,142 --> 00:28:31,310
Yes.

447
00:28:36,782 --> 00:28:39,051
By the way, who is this?

448
00:28:39,117 --> 00:28:40,852
-Min-gi.
-Min-gi?

449
00:28:40,919 --> 00:28:45,123
If I had a dad,
I think he'd be just like Min-gi.

450
00:28:45,190 --> 00:28:46,425
What?

451
00:28:46,491 --> 00:28:50,295
I told her that wasn't it,
but maybe it's… sympathy?

452
00:28:50,362 --> 00:28:53,031
A kind of pity?

453
00:28:53,098 --> 00:28:54,933
Something like that.

454
00:29:02,741 --> 00:29:06,745
Hold on. Hey, you look like a witch…

455
00:29:07,379 --> 00:29:10,549
That's not it! Hey, that's not it!

456
00:29:24,896 --> 00:29:26,365
Where are we even going?

457
00:29:26,431 --> 00:29:28,033
I'm so exhausted, I'm dying.

458
00:29:28,100 --> 00:29:29,534
We are almost there.

459
00:29:31,937 --> 00:29:33,572
Take a look here.

460
00:29:34,473 --> 00:29:35,907
What is this?

461
00:29:37,542 --> 00:29:40,712
-It's wild ginseng.
-Wild ginseng? Really?

462
00:29:41,380 --> 00:29:44,116
Judging by its size,
it looks about 50 years old.

463
00:29:44,182 --> 00:29:45,751
Fifty years?

464
00:29:46,818 --> 00:29:49,788
Wow, I've never seen
50-year-old wild ginseng in person.

465
00:29:49,855 --> 00:29:52,924
But why are you showing me this?

466
00:29:52,991 --> 00:29:54,660
Whoa!

467
00:29:56,161 --> 00:29:57,629
It's your birthday gift.

468
00:29:57,696 --> 00:30:01,967
You'd give me 50-year-old wild ginseng
for my birthday?

469
00:30:02,034 --> 00:30:04,036
This is a little too much, though.

470
00:30:04,102 --> 00:30:07,806
It's not for you.
It's for you to give to your parents.

471
00:30:07,873 --> 00:30:10,442
My parents? Why?

472
00:30:10,509 --> 00:30:13,378
A birthday gift isn't given
to the birthday person,

473
00:30:13,445 --> 00:30:15,280
but to their parents.

474
00:30:15,347 --> 00:30:18,183
All you did was be born.
What else did you do?

475
00:30:18,250 --> 00:30:21,553
Tell your parents,
"Thank you for giving birth to me,"

476
00:30:22,354 --> 00:30:23,989
and go give it to them.

477
00:30:24,589 --> 00:30:26,224
Hwa-ran.

478
00:30:31,930 --> 00:30:33,565
Freeze!

479
00:30:34,833 --> 00:30:36,468
Why?

480
00:30:46,778 --> 00:30:48,380
What are you doing?

481
00:30:48,447 --> 00:30:50,048
Hwa-ran, where are you going?

482
00:30:50,115 --> 00:30:52,084
She's so fast, jeez.

483
00:30:56,722 --> 00:30:58,256
Why is she so fast?

484
00:31:00,192 --> 00:31:02,294
It's a pheasant! A pheasant!

485
00:31:05,297 --> 00:31:07,833
What? Stay back, stay back!
Get that away!

486
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:11,002
-What is this?
-This one's a gift for you.

487
00:31:11,870 --> 00:31:13,372
No, thanks!

488
00:31:13,438 --> 00:31:15,307
It touched my hand! Forget it!

489
00:31:15,374 --> 00:31:17,509
This is really delicious roasted.

490
00:31:17,576 --> 00:31:19,778
Right, sounds delicious. Have plenty.

491
00:31:20,512 --> 00:31:22,714
Oh? There's another one!

492
00:31:26,651 --> 00:31:30,889
Gosh, she's a female Kim Byung-man.
A total female Kim Byung-man.

493
00:31:33,225 --> 00:31:35,894
If I married her, I'd never starve.

494
00:31:37,996 --> 00:31:40,132
What am I even saying right now?

495
00:31:50,175 --> 00:31:51,710
It's a kite!

496
00:31:54,980 --> 00:31:58,216
I'm great at making kites!
Hey, come quick! Hurry!

497
00:31:58,283 --> 00:31:59,785
Gather round!

498
00:32:01,953 --> 00:32:04,923
Mom! Min-gi made a kite for me!

499
00:32:04,990 --> 00:32:06,758
It flies so well!

500
00:32:21,907 --> 00:32:23,341
Talk about what?

501
00:32:24,976 --> 00:32:29,181
I wish you wouldn't be
too nice to Min-ho.

502
00:32:29,247 --> 00:32:30,515
-Huh?
-You mean well.

503
00:32:30,582 --> 00:32:32,451
You're just being nice, I know.

504
00:32:32,517 --> 00:32:34,619
But a kid gets the wrong idea.

505
00:32:35,153 --> 00:32:38,156
The wrong idea? What wrong idea?

506
00:32:40,225 --> 00:32:43,295
Min-ho drew a picture
at school yesterday.

507
00:32:43,962 --> 00:32:46,465
He drew you in his family portrait.

508
00:32:46,531 --> 00:32:48,633
He said if he had a dad,

509
00:32:48,700 --> 00:32:51,136
he'd be just like you, so he drew you.

510
00:32:51,203 --> 00:32:54,339
-So what?
-You're leaving soon.

511
00:32:54,406 --> 00:32:56,541
He likes you so much. What'll you do?

512
00:32:56,608 --> 00:32:58,343
I mean, that's…

513
00:32:58,410 --> 00:33:01,980
When someone keeps being nice to you,

514
00:33:02,047 --> 00:33:05,016
it's natural to get the wrong idea.

515
00:33:05,083 --> 00:33:06,885
You keep getting your hopes up,

516
00:33:07,619 --> 00:33:09,421
leaning on them,

517
00:33:10,188 --> 00:33:11,923
and wanting more.

518
00:33:16,094 --> 00:33:18,396
I'm not saying it's your fault.

519
00:33:18,463 --> 00:33:21,733
It's just the fault of the one
who leans and hopes for more.

520
00:33:22,567 --> 00:33:26,304
So don't be so nice to Min-ho anymore.

521
00:33:26,371 --> 00:33:28,073
Or to me.

522
00:33:29,508 --> 00:33:31,276
Please.

523
00:33:39,017 --> 00:33:41,553
What did I do wrong this time?

524
00:33:42,787 --> 00:33:44,589
Darn it.

525
00:33:46,358 --> 00:33:49,194
This is definitely the right village.

526
00:33:49,861 --> 00:33:52,964
Why isn't this kid Ki-jun picking up?

527
00:33:56,167 --> 00:33:57,502
Excuse me!

528
00:33:58,169 --> 00:34:01,873
May I ask you something?

529
00:34:01,940 --> 00:34:05,644
Do you happen to know
where Han Ki-jun lives?

530
00:34:05,710 --> 00:34:07,078
Han Ki-jun?

531
00:34:07,646 --> 00:34:09,981
Han Ki-jun, Ki-jun, Ki-jun, Ki-jun!

532
00:34:10,048 --> 00:34:11,983
-Yes!
-Let's share your umbrella.

533
00:34:12,050 --> 00:34:15,287
Oh, my goodness. Sure, okay.

534
00:34:29,034 --> 00:34:31,202
-Welcome home, Min-ho.
-Oh, you're back?

535
00:34:31,269 --> 00:34:32,504
You came with Mom.

536
00:34:33,338 --> 00:34:36,341
Yes, we'll wash up quickly
and get the meal ready.

537
00:34:36,413 --> 00:34:38,043
-Okay.
-All right.

538
00:34:44,883 --> 00:34:47,953
Oh my, Man-gu, what brings you here?

539
00:34:48,019 --> 00:34:51,222
Well, someone came looking for Ki-jun.

540
00:34:51,289 --> 00:34:52,424
Please come in.

541
00:34:58,797 --> 00:35:01,299
Ma'am! Hello!

542
00:35:01,366 --> 00:35:04,069
Oh my, Min-gi! Hyeok!

543
00:35:04,135 --> 00:35:05,637
Why are you two here?

544
00:35:05,704 --> 00:35:09,441
Are you two here with Ki-jun
to study for the civil service exam?

545
00:35:12,310 --> 00:35:14,479
Yes, yes! That's right.

546
00:35:14,546 --> 00:35:16,514
-The civil service exam, yes.
-Yes.

547
00:35:16,581 --> 00:35:20,251
But Hyeok, you're a med student.
Why take the civil service exam?

548
00:35:20,318 --> 00:35:23,622
Well, even doctors struggle
to make a living these days.

549
00:35:23,688 --> 00:35:26,257
Above all else,
a civil service job is the best!

550
00:35:26,324 --> 00:35:27,425
Yes, indeed.

551
00:35:27,492 --> 00:35:29,728
Excuse me, but who are you…?

552
00:35:29,794 --> 00:35:32,063
-She's Ki-jun's mom.
-Oh, Ki-jun's mom?

553
00:35:32,130 --> 00:35:34,466
Gosh, Ki-jun must take after his dad--

554
00:35:34,532 --> 00:35:35,834
Um… Hello.

555
00:35:35,900 --> 00:35:37,702
Yes, hello there!

556
00:35:37,769 --> 00:35:39,437
By the way, who is he?

557
00:35:42,107 --> 00:35:43,975
Oh!

558
00:35:44,042 --> 00:35:46,177
He's… the study lodge owner.

559
00:35:46,244 --> 00:35:47,679
The owner?

560
00:35:47,746 --> 00:35:50,915
Yes, well, this is a study lodge.

561
00:35:50,982 --> 00:35:53,785
A custom rural study lodge.

562
00:35:53,852 --> 00:35:55,854
A rural study lodge?

563
00:35:55,920 --> 00:35:57,689
There's such a thing?

564
00:35:58,556 --> 00:36:01,092
You haven't heard? It's all the rage.

565
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:04,429
Instead of the bleak city,
the fresh country air here

566
00:36:04,496 --> 00:36:07,065
helps you study with a clear mind.

567
00:36:07,132 --> 00:36:09,267
Call it a new-concept study lodge.

568
00:36:09,334 --> 00:36:11,336
Oh, really?

569
00:36:12,037 --> 00:36:14,139
But why are you two dressed like that?

570
00:36:14,205 --> 00:36:16,041
You look like farmers.

571
00:36:17,208 --> 00:36:19,644
Well, you see, that's…

572
00:36:20,311 --> 00:36:23,615
Oh! Whenever we're studying

573
00:36:23,682 --> 00:36:27,719
and get tired,
we tend this little vegetable garden.

574
00:36:27,786 --> 00:36:30,555
They say it's a huge help for focus.

575
00:36:30,622 --> 00:36:33,291
-To help us focus.
-Anyway, what brings you here?

576
00:36:33,358 --> 00:36:35,960
I came because it's Ki-jun's birthday.

577
00:36:36,027 --> 00:36:37,595
It's my baby boy's birthday.

578
00:36:37,662 --> 00:36:39,364
I should make him seaweed soup.

579
00:36:39,431 --> 00:36:41,499
By the way, where did Ki-jun go?

580
00:36:42,233 --> 00:36:44,436
-He's out. We'll go…
-Let's go get him.

581
00:36:44,502 --> 00:36:46,705
-We'll go get him.
-No, no, it's fine.

582
00:36:46,771 --> 00:36:48,707
He'll be back soon. Let's go in.

583
00:36:48,773 --> 00:36:50,241
Go inside?

584
00:36:50,875 --> 00:36:52,277
-Yes, yes, ma'am.
-Yes.

585
00:36:52,343 --> 00:36:54,379
Here, give me that. Let me take it.

586
00:36:59,050 --> 00:37:01,319
Wow, these pork trotters are delicious.

587
00:37:01,386 --> 00:37:02,687
You think so?

588
00:37:02,754 --> 00:37:06,024
Actually, we run a pork trotter shop.

589
00:37:06,091 --> 00:37:08,126
I told him to just take over the shop,

590
00:37:08,193 --> 00:37:10,829
but he's dead set
on the civil service exam,

591
00:37:10,895 --> 00:37:13,498
so I'm worried sick about him.

592
00:37:13,565 --> 00:37:15,166
Please eat plenty, everyone.

593
00:37:15,233 --> 00:37:18,103
Please take good care of Ki-jun, sir.

594
00:37:18,169 --> 00:37:20,038
Pardon?

595
00:37:20,105 --> 00:37:22,073
Uh, yes, of course.

596
00:37:24,442 --> 00:37:27,746
Where did Ki-jun go? Why isn't he back?

597
00:37:27,812 --> 00:37:29,714
He won't answer his phone either.

598
00:37:30,715 --> 00:37:34,219
He can't answer while studying.
He's concentrating too hard.

599
00:37:34,285 --> 00:37:35,353
Really?

600
00:37:35,420 --> 00:37:37,122
I can't wait around forever.

601
00:37:37,789 --> 00:37:40,458
I have work tomorrow, so I should go.

602
00:37:40,525 --> 00:37:42,794
Are you sure you have to go?

603
00:37:42,861 --> 00:37:44,596
Then let's head out right away.

604
00:37:44,662 --> 00:37:46,698
Okay, sure. Goodness.

605
00:37:49,968 --> 00:37:52,170
Go on back inside now.

606
00:37:52,237 --> 00:37:54,773
Make sure you all study hard, too.

607
00:37:54,839 --> 00:37:56,574
Yes, we're sure to pass, right?

608
00:37:56,641 --> 00:37:58,576
Right, don't worry.

609
00:37:59,677 --> 00:38:00,912
-All right.
-Hwa-ran.

610
00:38:00,979 --> 00:38:03,081
Shame we couldn't catch that boar too.

611
00:38:05,316 --> 00:38:07,619
Oh my! Ki-jun!

612
00:38:09,687 --> 00:38:12,123
-Uh, Mom.
-Hey!

613
00:38:12,190 --> 00:38:14,159
Where have you been?

614
00:38:14,225 --> 00:38:15,527
Huh?

615
00:38:15,593 --> 00:38:17,896
And what's with the way you look?

616
00:38:18,563 --> 00:38:20,431
Weren't you out studying?

617
00:38:21,199 --> 00:38:23,501
Uh… I was, but the thing is…

618
00:38:27,038 --> 00:38:29,240
And who is this woman?

619
00:38:32,076 --> 00:38:35,346
Oh, she's his Chinese teacher. Laoshi.

620
00:38:36,281 --> 00:38:38,116
Hwa-ran, say hi to Ki-jun's mom.

621
00:38:38,183 --> 00:38:39,617
She's my mom.

622
00:38:39,684 --> 00:38:41,686
Uh… Ni hao ma.

623
00:38:41,753 --> 00:38:43,855
Oh, yes.

624
00:38:44,656 --> 00:38:46,891
Why Chinese for the civil service exam?

625
00:38:46,958 --> 00:38:50,395
Huh? Well, that's because…

626
00:38:50,461 --> 00:38:52,363
These days, civil servants need

627
00:38:52,430 --> 00:38:55,266
at least one mandatory second language.

628
00:38:55,333 --> 00:38:57,068
Bonus points! Bam, bam, bam!

629
00:38:57,135 --> 00:38:59,037
-Bam, bam, bam!
-Bonus points!

630
00:38:59,637 --> 00:39:02,006
So I've been studying Chinese lately…

631
00:39:02,674 --> 00:39:05,877
-But Mom, what brings you here?
-Well…

632
00:39:05,944 --> 00:39:09,447
It's your birthday, so I packed
seaweed soup and pork trotters.

633
00:39:09,514 --> 00:39:11,950
I waited for you, but my bus is soon,

634
00:39:12,016 --> 00:39:13,952
so I was just on my way out.

635
00:39:14,953 --> 00:39:16,688
-I see.
-Still, I'm glad.

636
00:39:16,754 --> 00:39:19,057
Seeing you work so hard is a relief.

637
00:39:19,123 --> 00:39:21,326
This study lodge feels so homey,

638
00:39:21,392 --> 00:39:24,195
and the couple who run it seem nice.

639
00:39:25,964 --> 00:39:27,632
A… study lodge?

640
00:39:31,269 --> 00:39:34,172
Oh, right! They're wonderful people.

641
00:39:34,239 --> 00:39:36,474
They treat me so well, like family.

642
00:39:36,541 --> 00:39:39,777
Good. Make sure you eat well, son.

643
00:39:39,844 --> 00:39:42,380
-Study hard and keep it up.
-Yes, Mom.

644
00:39:42,447 --> 00:39:44,182
Mom, I'll walk you. It's close.

645
00:39:44,249 --> 00:39:46,618
No, no, no. I'll go by myself.

646
00:39:46,684 --> 00:39:49,053
Go back and study your Chinese hard.

647
00:39:49,120 --> 00:39:51,723
-I'm off now.
-Bye! Zaijian!

648
00:39:51,789 --> 00:39:54,125
I said that in Chinese! In Chinese!

649
00:39:54,759 --> 00:39:56,394
Get home safely, ma'am.

650
00:39:59,998 --> 00:40:01,933
Jeez, I thought we were so busted.

651
00:40:02,000 --> 00:40:03,835
Where have you been, seriously?

652
00:40:03,902 --> 00:40:05,403
Just around here…

653
00:40:10,642 --> 00:40:14,212
Man, I still feel guilty toward Mom.

654
00:40:17,515 --> 00:40:20,652
I think the bus stop was around here.

655
00:40:20,718 --> 00:40:22,553
This is confusing.

656
00:40:22,620 --> 00:40:24,455
I should ask someone.

657
00:40:24,522 --> 00:40:26,858
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

658
00:40:26,925 --> 00:40:30,028
-What is it?
-Where is the bus stop?

659
00:40:30,094 --> 00:40:34,032
The bus stop? Just go a bit this way.

660
00:40:34,098 --> 00:40:37,302
By the way, who are you?
I haven't seen you before.

661
00:40:37,368 --> 00:40:41,172
Me? I'm… Over at
the rural study lodge that way,

662
00:40:41,239 --> 00:40:43,775
do you know Ki-jun,
studying for civil exams?

663
00:40:43,841 --> 00:40:45,910
I'm his mother.

664
00:40:45,977 --> 00:40:47,812
Ki-jun, the civil exam student?

665
00:40:47,879 --> 00:40:50,148
Oh! Bul-ja's groom!

666
00:40:51,316 --> 00:40:53,351
What do you mean, Bul-ja?

667
00:40:53,418 --> 00:40:57,121
Bul-ja… Oh, that Chinese teacher!

668
00:40:57,188 --> 00:40:59,624
A Chinese teacher? She's not.

669
00:41:00,291 --> 00:41:02,660
She's not? Then who is she?

670
00:41:02,727 --> 00:41:06,030
It's a secret, so keep it to yourself.

671
00:41:06,097 --> 00:41:07,999
You see, that Bul-ja is…

672
00:41:18,476 --> 00:41:20,845
Our pork trotters are as good as ever!

673
00:41:21,479 --> 00:41:25,483
Thanks, Mom. I'll really pay you back
once I make money selling cabbages.

674
00:41:25,550 --> 00:41:28,519
Ki-jun, even we had to lie for you.

675
00:41:28,586 --> 00:41:30,955
Gosh, I felt so guilty, it was rough.

676
00:41:31,022 --> 00:41:32,590
I'm really sorry.

677
00:41:32,657 --> 00:41:34,959
Glad it went well.
What if we got caught?

678
00:41:36,794 --> 00:41:40,698
No, not that. My life… Thank goodness.

679
00:41:47,672 --> 00:41:48,806
What is it?

680
00:41:52,176 --> 00:41:53,378
Hey!

681
00:41:53,945 --> 00:41:58,282
Han Ki-jun, you crazy bastard!

682
00:42:00,184 --> 00:42:01,519
Mom.

683
00:42:01,586 --> 00:42:03,654
What? A study lodge?

684
00:42:03,721 --> 00:42:06,224
A Chinese teacher?

685
00:42:06,290 --> 00:42:07,558
You little brat!

686
00:42:16,401 --> 00:42:18,169
Ow, ow! Mom, Mom!

687
00:42:18,236 --> 00:42:19,937
I'm sorry! I'm really sorry!

688
00:42:20,004 --> 00:42:23,408
You said you'd study for civil exams,
and you farm cabbage?

689
00:42:23,474 --> 00:42:25,710
And even dating an illegal immigrant?

690
00:42:25,777 --> 00:42:27,245
Are you out of your mind?

691
00:42:27,945 --> 00:42:30,348
Mom, just hear me out first. Listen…

692
00:42:30,415 --> 00:42:31,983
There's nothing to hear.

693
00:42:32,050 --> 00:42:34,986
Go back to Seoul now
and work at the pork trotter shop.

694
00:42:35,053 --> 00:42:38,289
No! I don't want to!

695
00:42:38,356 --> 00:42:41,025
-I'm not going to Seoul.
-What, you little brat?

696
00:42:41,793 --> 00:42:43,761
I don't want the pork trotter shop,

697
00:42:43,828 --> 00:42:46,297
or be a damn civil servant.
It doesn't suit me.

698
00:42:46,364 --> 00:42:48,699
Now I want to live doing what I want.

699
00:42:48,766 --> 00:42:50,435
I don't care or want to do it.

700
00:42:50,501 --> 00:42:52,437
I forced myself since everyone does…

701
00:42:52,503 --> 00:42:55,440
I'm sick of just following others now.

702
00:42:57,909 --> 00:42:59,444
What I'm doing out here…

703
00:43:00,311 --> 00:43:02,914
must seem immature and foolish to you.

704
00:43:02,980 --> 00:43:05,950
But you know what, Mom?

705
00:43:06,017 --> 00:43:07,819
I'm really happy these days.

706
00:43:09,420 --> 00:43:13,057
For once, I feel like I'm truly alive.

707
00:43:14,492 --> 00:43:15,893
So…

708
00:43:17,695 --> 00:43:19,197
can't you just trust me,

709
00:43:20,198 --> 00:43:22,767
trust me and let me be, okay?

710
00:43:22,834 --> 00:43:24,035
I'm begging you, Mom.

711
00:43:24,102 --> 00:43:27,238
Ugh, you damn brat.

712
00:43:27,305 --> 00:43:29,874
Do what you want! Do what you want!

713
00:43:31,742 --> 00:43:33,211
Mom.

714
00:43:34,045 --> 00:43:35,646
Mom!

715
00:43:48,226 --> 00:43:49,861
Mom.

716
00:43:50,828 --> 00:43:52,497
I'm sorry.

717
00:43:59,137 --> 00:44:00,938
Mom, Mom, Mom!

718
00:44:01,005 --> 00:44:02,773
What, what, what, what?

719
00:44:09,313 --> 00:44:10,948
What's this?

720
00:44:11,015 --> 00:44:13,718
Wild ginseng, 50 years old.

721
00:44:13,784 --> 00:44:17,522
Wild ginseng? Why give this to me?

722
00:44:17,588 --> 00:44:19,657
Someone told me

723
00:44:20,324 --> 00:44:23,694
on your birthday, you should
celebrate your parents instead.

724
00:44:23,761 --> 00:44:26,397
I wouldn't have a birthday without you.

725
00:44:26,964 --> 00:44:28,699
Mom.

726
00:44:29,800 --> 00:44:31,736
Thank you for giving birth to me.

727
00:44:32,703 --> 00:44:34,939
Oh, you little troublemaker.

728
00:44:41,679 --> 00:44:43,247
Mom!

729
00:44:44,048 --> 00:44:46,784
I'll really succeed
and really take care of you!

730
00:44:46,851 --> 00:44:48,719
Forget it, you brat.

731
00:44:48,786 --> 00:44:50,888
Just keep it a secret from Dad, kid.

732
00:44:50,955 --> 00:44:54,192
And if you don't take care of me later,
you're dead meat.

733
00:45:00,264 --> 00:45:02,633
Mom, I'll really take care of you!

734
00:45:02,700 --> 00:45:04,769
Get home safe, Mom!

735
00:45:04,835 --> 00:45:06,904
I love you, Mom!

736
00:45:06,971 --> 00:45:08,739
Bye!

737
00:45:35,800 --> 00:45:37,368
Mother.

738
00:45:37,435 --> 00:45:40,738
You're such a wonderful cook.

739
00:45:41,372 --> 00:45:44,375
Really? I'm glad it suits your taste.

740
00:45:44,442 --> 00:45:46,711
-Please have plenty.
-Yes, thank you.

741
00:45:49,714 --> 00:45:51,816
Anyway, how long are you staying here?

742
00:45:51,882 --> 00:45:55,119
-Aren't you going home?
-Why do you keep rushing her home?

743
00:45:55,786 --> 00:45:58,522
Don't go. It's too late,
so please stay the night.

744
00:45:58,589 --> 00:46:00,258
What are you talking about?

745
00:46:00,324 --> 00:46:03,094
-Why would Bong-ryeon…
-Yes, I'll stay the night.

746
00:46:03,160 --> 00:46:06,697
Oh, my head is so dizzy,
I don't think I can even get up.

747
00:46:08,766 --> 00:46:11,002
Su-yeon must be really sick, though.

748
00:46:11,068 --> 00:46:13,237
She hasn't budged all day.

749
00:46:23,914 --> 00:46:26,851
Oh, you're awake?

750
00:46:26,917 --> 00:46:28,686
How are you feeling?

751
00:46:31,689 --> 00:46:33,391
I feel much better.

752
00:46:36,227 --> 00:46:37,995
But why is this guy here…

753
00:46:38,062 --> 00:46:40,464
That guy nursed you all night.

754
00:46:40,531 --> 00:46:44,435
He didn't sleep a wink
and stayed right by your side.

755
00:46:44,502 --> 00:46:47,104
I took him for a psycho and a pervert.

756
00:46:47,171 --> 00:46:50,508
But he's actually quite devoted.

757
00:46:51,275 --> 00:46:52,677
Really?

758
00:46:54,312 --> 00:46:56,013
Han-cheol.

759
00:46:56,080 --> 00:46:58,716
Han-cheol, please wake up!

760
00:46:58,783 --> 00:46:59,950
Oh my!

761
00:47:00,017 --> 00:47:02,420
-What? What's wrong with him?
-Han-cheol!

762
00:47:07,258 --> 00:47:08,826
He's burning up.

763
00:47:12,263 --> 00:47:14,065
I think he caught your cold.

764
00:47:14,965 --> 00:47:16,167
What?

765
00:47:16,233 --> 00:47:20,037
Jeez, just from nursing you,
he already caught your cold.

766
00:47:20,104 --> 00:47:22,740
Good grief, you hopeless fool.

767
00:47:23,441 --> 00:47:25,109
I'm cold.

768
00:47:25,843 --> 00:47:27,411
I'm cold.

769
00:47:35,152 --> 00:47:37,388
You went to nurse her and got her cold.

770
00:47:38,155 --> 00:47:39,557
Well done, sir.

771
00:47:39,623 --> 00:47:41,492
Hey, shut up.

772
00:47:42,560 --> 00:47:44,161
Just get me another blanket.

773
00:47:44,228 --> 00:47:46,230
I'm cold, so cold right now. Really.

774
00:47:46,297 --> 00:47:47,998
We're cold too.

775
00:47:48,065 --> 00:47:51,135
Hey, she won't even appreciate it,

776
00:47:51,202 --> 00:47:53,471
so why risk your life for that woman?

777
00:47:53,537 --> 00:47:57,241
Hey, love isn't about expecting
to get back as much as you give.

778
00:47:57,308 --> 00:48:01,245
It's about giving unconditionally,
just giving, you punk!

779
00:48:02,246 --> 00:48:04,482
The grand poet has graced us.

780
00:48:04,548 --> 00:48:07,385
Still, you got a cold, so you're even.

781
00:48:07,451 --> 00:48:09,353
Anyway,

782
00:48:09,420 --> 00:48:13,691
I wonder if she's ready for tomorrow's
Paldo Gangsan Singing Contest prelims.

783
00:48:14,859 --> 00:48:17,762
Whatever. She said she'd handle it.

784
00:48:20,631 --> 00:48:23,300
Oh? Sister-in-law?

785
00:48:23,367 --> 00:48:26,270
Wait, sister-in-law?

786
00:48:26,337 --> 00:48:28,372
Su-yeon! Su-yeon!

787
00:48:30,374 --> 00:48:33,778
Hello, Su-yeon. What brings you here?

788
00:48:33,844 --> 00:48:36,580
I just brought you some porridge.

789
00:48:38,883 --> 00:48:40,885
Porridge?

790
00:48:40,951 --> 00:48:43,821
You made it for me yourself? Really?

791
00:48:45,022 --> 00:48:47,091
I should get going then.

792
00:48:54,298 --> 00:48:57,234
Hey, did you see that? Did you see it?

793
00:48:57,301 --> 00:48:59,904
Su-yeon made porridge just for me!

794
00:48:59,970 --> 00:49:03,274
She made it herself! Handmade! Wow!

795
00:49:05,543 --> 00:49:07,044
Gosh, are you that happy?

796
00:49:07,111 --> 00:49:09,046
Of course I am! Why wouldn't I be?

797
00:49:12,516 --> 00:49:14,885
Hey, wipe your snot before eating, man!

798
00:49:14,952 --> 00:49:17,621
So what? It's my own snot.

799
00:50:30,628 --> 00:50:33,397
PALDO GANGSAN SINGING CONTEST
PRELIMINARIES

800
00:50:33,464 --> 00:50:35,926
CONTESTANTS, PLEASE WAIT IN THE LOBBY

801
00:50:37,101 --> 00:50:40,404
Anyway, will Yu-na be okay alone?
I'm worried about her.

802
00:50:40,471 --> 00:50:43,240
Is Yu-na a child?
She can't even stay home alone?

803
00:50:43,307 --> 00:50:45,042
Why not put her in your pocket?

804
00:50:45,109 --> 00:50:46,877
I'm just worried, that's all.

805
00:50:47,878 --> 00:50:51,081
-Did your mom say she got home?
-Yes, she said she made it.

806
00:50:51,148 --> 00:50:53,918
Right, Hwa-ran.
Mom says thanks for the wild ginseng.

807
00:50:54,518 --> 00:50:57,488
Not at all, it was nothing, really…

808
00:50:58,055 --> 00:51:00,057
Wild ginseng? You said wild ginseng?

809
00:51:00,124 --> 00:51:02,693
Yes, Hwa-ran gave me
wild ginseng on my birthday.

810
00:51:02,760 --> 00:51:04,228
A 50-year-old one.

811
00:51:05,296 --> 00:51:08,032
She gave you wild ginseng
for your birthday?

812
00:51:08,098 --> 00:51:10,467
Wow, she goes big. Really big.

813
00:51:10,534 --> 00:51:12,937
She's got the blood of the continent!

814
00:51:13,003 --> 00:51:14,605
Oh, right, ma'am.

815
00:51:14,672 --> 00:51:16,941
I heard you told my mom everything?

816
00:51:17,007 --> 00:51:19,176
What? I have no idea what you mean.

817
00:51:19,243 --> 00:51:21,812
I heard it all from Mom.
She said you told her.

818
00:51:21,879 --> 00:51:23,480
Ugh, I said it was a secret.

819
00:51:23,547 --> 00:51:25,249
Why is your mom so loose-lipped?

820
00:51:25,316 --> 00:51:27,518
You're the most loose-lipped of all.

821
00:51:27,585 --> 00:51:31,221
Anyway, just so you know,
I'll get back at you someday.

822
00:51:31,922 --> 00:51:34,925
Well, anyway, is Yun-hui
getting ready all right?

823
00:51:34,992 --> 00:51:36,827
She just has to pass, I reckon.

824
00:51:36,894 --> 00:51:40,364
Don't even get your hopes up.
She didn't even practice.

825
00:51:40,431 --> 00:51:43,200
Anyway, she's just ridiculously proud.

826
00:51:43,267 --> 00:51:44,768
Anyway, didn't Man-gu come?

827
00:51:44,835 --> 00:51:48,005
Not sure, he left early this morning.

828
00:51:49,273 --> 00:51:50,774
Gosh, isn't that Sang-deuk?

829
00:51:52,309 --> 00:51:54,979
Why keep following me?
Go home if you're sober now.

830
00:51:55,045 --> 00:51:58,983
Your mother told me
to look around with you before I go.

831
00:51:59,049 --> 00:52:01,619
Besides, I have nothing to do at home.

832
00:52:01,685 --> 00:52:04,254
Have nothing to do?
Go to a host bar you like.

833
00:52:04,321 --> 00:52:06,357
They aren't even open yet…

834
00:52:07,458 --> 00:52:09,693
What do you mean? I don't go there.

835
00:52:09,760 --> 00:52:12,796
Goodness, Sang-deuk, who is she?

836
00:52:12,863 --> 00:52:14,064
Hello.

837
00:52:14,131 --> 00:52:17,701
I'm Lee Bong-ryeon,
and I'm seriously dating Sang-deuk.

838
00:52:17,768 --> 00:52:21,372
What are you talking about?
Who is seriously dating who?

839
00:52:21,438 --> 00:52:24,541
Playing hard to get again, you tease!

840
00:52:25,242 --> 00:52:28,545
-Ow, my nose hurts!
-Why did you touch me?

841
00:52:31,882 --> 00:52:34,551
Hey, Mi-yeong, Sang-deuk is here too.

842
00:52:36,520 --> 00:52:39,823
-What about the shop?
-I closed it briefly to come watch.

843
00:52:39,890 --> 00:52:41,225
Mi-yeong, um…

844
00:52:43,927 --> 00:52:46,230
-I-ji, let's go inside.
-Okay.

845
00:52:46,296 --> 00:52:47,464
Mi-yeong.

846
00:52:48,999 --> 00:52:51,769
This is driving me crazy, seriously.

847
00:52:51,835 --> 00:52:55,806
Still playing hard to get?
Sang-deuk, let's go together.

848
00:52:55,873 --> 00:52:57,708
What's with that woman's laugh?

849
00:52:57,775 --> 00:52:59,476
I know, I can't even copy it.

850
00:53:19,930 --> 00:53:21,432
Wow.

851
00:53:22,199 --> 00:53:24,301
Is that really Yun-hui?

852
00:53:24,368 --> 00:53:28,372
My goodness, look who it is!
You look like a whole new person.

853
00:53:28,439 --> 00:53:32,810
Really? I feel so awkward
in all this. Goodness, I swear…

854
00:53:32,876 --> 00:53:34,545
Not at all, Yun-hui.

855
00:53:34,611 --> 00:53:36,847
Dressed up, you look totally different!

856
00:53:36,914 --> 00:53:38,549
Right, Min-gi?

857
00:53:38,615 --> 00:53:40,150
Huh?

858
00:53:40,217 --> 00:53:42,686
Well, at least she looks ladylike.

859
00:53:42,753 --> 00:53:45,522
What do you mean? She looks so pretty.

860
00:53:45,589 --> 00:53:46,957
Good luck, Yun-hui.

861
00:53:47,624 --> 00:53:48,992
Thanks.

862
00:53:49,059 --> 00:53:51,095
I'll head inside first and get ready.

863
00:53:51,161 --> 00:53:53,664
Alright, do your best! Go for it!

864
00:53:56,333 --> 00:54:00,671
They say clothes make the woman.
A woman's got to dress up, goodness.

865
00:54:04,408 --> 00:54:06,310
Nice to meet you all.

866
00:54:15,185 --> 00:54:17,020
Mommy!

867
00:54:17,087 --> 00:54:18,889
Thank you for all that passion.

868
00:54:18,956 --> 00:54:21,492
Now let's meet our next contestant.

869
00:54:21,558 --> 00:54:23,494
Give them a big round of applause.

870
00:54:24,862 --> 00:54:27,998
Huh? Isn't that Mr. Man-gu?

871
00:54:28,499 --> 00:54:29,733
How do you do?

872
00:54:29,798 --> 00:54:33,570
I'm Hwang Man-gu of Hadurok-ri,
Indi County, here to greet you all.

873
00:54:33,637 --> 00:54:35,305
Man-gu's up there.

874
00:54:35,372 --> 00:54:36,440
Good grief.

875
00:54:36,507 --> 00:54:40,310
He wouldn't accept the verdict,
and just had to enter on his own.

876
00:54:40,377 --> 00:54:42,346
PALDO GANGSAN INDI COUNTY PRELIMS

877
00:54:43,313 --> 00:54:46,383
-Boom, boom! I'm here!
-Oh, no.

878
00:54:46,450 --> 00:54:48,519
Thank you, and great job out there.

879
00:54:48,585 --> 00:54:50,621
We'll move on to the next contestant.

880
00:54:50,687 --> 00:54:53,190
Please come out. Give her a big hand!

881
00:54:56,860 --> 00:54:58,228
It's Yun-hui!

882
00:54:58,295 --> 00:55:00,264
Hey, guys, wake up!

883
00:55:00,330 --> 00:55:02,166
Yun-hui's on stage, Min-gi!

884
00:55:11,708 --> 00:55:15,846
Have you forgotten me?

885
00:55:17,815 --> 00:55:22,319
Those burning eyes

886
00:55:24,321 --> 00:55:26,990
Have you forgotten

887
00:55:27,057 --> 00:55:29,626
Those days we shared

888
00:55:30,294 --> 00:55:34,865
And our beautiful memories?

889
00:55:36,633 --> 00:55:40,971
Even though we loved each other

890
00:55:43,140 --> 00:55:46,677
We could not even meet

891
00:55:49,146 --> 00:55:52,115
Oh, no! My money, my money! Oh, no!

892
00:55:52,182 --> 00:55:53,617
Hey, call the police now!

893
00:55:53,684 --> 00:55:55,152
Come on, just stop already!

894
00:55:55,219 --> 00:55:57,888
Stupid money, money, money!
Does money matter now?

895
00:55:57,955 --> 00:56:00,257
We need to get you to a hospital first!

896
00:56:05,929 --> 00:56:07,931
Oh, no!

897
00:56:08,699 --> 00:56:10,300
I swear.

898
00:56:30,254 --> 00:56:34,725
Must we part ways once again

899
00:56:36,627 --> 00:56:40,564
With our pain tucked away

900
00:56:42,299 --> 00:56:46,637
Must we walk away once again?

901
00:56:48,572 --> 00:56:52,743
Leaving me all alone

902
00:56:54,811 --> 00:56:58,448
Leaving me all…

903
00:56:59,349 --> 00:57:01,585
Alone

904
00:57:10,193 --> 00:57:12,896
-She's got a great vibe.
-I think she'll pass.

905
00:57:21,138 --> 00:57:23,840
No matter how I look at it,
this makes no sense.

906
00:57:23,907 --> 00:57:27,044
How could Yun-hui fail and Man-gu pass?

907
00:57:27,110 --> 00:57:29,179
It makes total sense, you punk!

908
00:57:29,246 --> 00:57:32,516
The esteemed judges saw my talent.

909
00:57:32,582 --> 00:57:35,552
What? My gaze is sleazy and amateurish?

910
00:57:35,619 --> 00:57:37,421
Ugh, you clueless jerks.

911
00:57:38,088 --> 00:57:40,924
Still, you saved my skin, Man-gu.

912
00:57:40,991 --> 00:57:42,125
Thank you.

913
00:57:42,192 --> 00:57:45,162
In return, make sure
you promote our apples well, okay?

914
00:57:45,228 --> 00:57:46,863
Don't you worry.

915
00:57:46,930 --> 00:57:50,867
I'll definitely feed
our Indi County apples to Song-hae.

916
00:57:50,934 --> 00:57:53,203
"Sir, have an apple!"

917
00:57:53,270 --> 00:57:56,073
I'm so proud of you, son, so proud.

918
00:57:56,139 --> 00:57:58,275
Really? Buy me something tasty, Mom.

919
00:57:58,342 --> 00:58:00,544
Okay, okay. Let's go, my baby.

920
00:58:00,610 --> 00:58:02,946
-Oh, my baby.
-I like the butt dance best.

921
00:58:04,848 --> 00:58:08,352
More than that guy
passing the preliminaries,

922
00:58:08,418 --> 00:58:11,621
the fact that those two
are mother and son

923
00:58:12,189 --> 00:58:14,124
is what I still can't believe.

924
00:58:14,191 --> 00:58:15,926
Anyway, you did great.

925
00:58:15,993 --> 00:58:17,327
Thanks.

926
00:58:17,394 --> 00:58:19,229
That's our Village Head!

927
00:58:19,296 --> 00:58:21,531
-A secret behind his birth?
-Definitely.

928
00:58:21,598 --> 00:58:23,166
Aren't they hiding something?

929
00:58:26,303 --> 00:58:28,772
But Min-gi, what's with your face?

930
00:58:29,473 --> 00:58:32,242
-No, it's nothing.
-Really?

931
00:58:32,309 --> 00:58:34,811
You guys worked hard cheering today.

932
00:58:34,878 --> 00:58:37,547
I'll buy you something good. Let's go.

933
00:58:37,614 --> 00:58:38,849
Huh?

934
00:58:38,915 --> 00:58:41,518
Why that reaction?
Don't you want something good?

935
00:58:42,252 --> 00:58:44,121
Come on, stop that and let's go.

936
00:58:44,187 --> 00:58:45,956
I'll buy something really good.

937
00:58:46,023 --> 00:58:47,924
Come on, let's go, let's go!

938
00:58:50,627 --> 00:58:53,663
PALDO GANGSAN SINGING CONTEST

939
00:58:53,730 --> 00:58:55,999
You all saw it there in person.

940
00:58:56,066 --> 00:58:58,435
Why make a fuss gathering to watch it?

941
00:58:58,502 --> 00:59:00,904
You're on TV, man.
We have to watch together.

942
00:59:00,971 --> 00:59:04,708
Right, it'll be fun to watch it again.

943
00:59:05,776 --> 00:59:07,677
Now, don't any of you laugh.

944
00:59:08,278 --> 00:59:09,613
Don't laugh!

945
00:59:09,679 --> 00:59:11,181
-Oh, he's on!
-There he is!

946
00:59:11,248 --> 00:59:14,317
Introducing Hwang Man-gu.
Please give him a big hand.

947
00:59:19,956 --> 00:59:22,893
You have to take the mic.
The mic, the mic.

948
01:00:17,848 --> 01:00:20,183
Let us bring out our next contestant.

949
01:00:20,817 --> 01:00:24,221
Mother, I love you! Father, I love you!

950
01:00:29,092 --> 01:00:31,094
How did he fall off right there?

951
01:00:33,396 --> 01:00:35,332
Stop laughing, everyone!

952
01:00:35,398 --> 01:00:36,833
Can't help it. It's funny.

953
01:00:36,900 --> 01:00:39,002
If only I hadn't worn that hat,

954
01:00:39,069 --> 01:00:41,438
I… Ugh, forget it!

955
01:00:41,505 --> 01:00:43,340
-Oh, my.
-Where are you going?

956
01:00:44,040 --> 01:00:46,543
I'm laughing my head off, I really am!

957
01:00:46,610 --> 01:00:49,179
Even just looking at him now is funny.

958
01:00:49,246 --> 01:00:51,515
Sure, this is funny and all, but

959
01:00:52,182 --> 01:00:54,985
what do we do since
we couldn't promote the apples?

960
01:00:55,051 --> 01:00:58,722
Please don't worry, I handled it all.

961
01:01:00,390 --> 01:01:04,094
This is a government site
that helps farmers do business.

962
01:01:04,161 --> 01:01:06,229
I asked how to sell Indi County apples,

963
01:01:06,296 --> 01:01:08,331
and they showed me this online store.

964
01:01:08,398 --> 01:01:11,968
And now the orders are pouring in,
just pouring right in!

965
01:01:12,569 --> 01:01:15,172
That's a relief, such a relief.

966
01:01:16,006 --> 01:01:17,908
You worked so hard, Yun-hui.

967
01:01:17,974 --> 01:01:20,777
It was nothing. I barely did a thing.

968
01:01:21,978 --> 01:01:24,214
Now then, let's all get to work, okay?

969
01:01:24,281 --> 01:01:28,251
Wow, the weather today
is fantastic, just fantastic!

970
01:01:28,318 --> 01:01:29,986
Right, Min-gi?

971
01:01:30,787 --> 01:01:32,622
Huh?

972
01:01:32,689 --> 01:01:34,457
Sure, it is.

973
01:01:35,091 --> 01:01:36,860
Yu-na, how about just us women

974
01:01:36,927 --> 01:01:38,495
grab some rice wine later?

975
01:01:38,562 --> 01:01:40,664
-Sure, sounds good.
-It's a deal!

976
01:01:40,730 --> 01:01:42,432
I can really hold my liquor,

977
01:01:42,499 --> 01:01:44,701
so you'd better brace yourself.

978
01:01:45,402 --> 01:01:47,304
I swear, that little punk…

979
01:01:47,370 --> 01:01:50,207
I'll tell you all about
how pathetic he used to be.

980
01:01:52,976 --> 01:01:55,912
Park Hong-gu, repeat three times
that you're dead today!

981
01:01:55,979 --> 01:01:58,648
We have a mountain of work today,
a real mountain!

982
01:01:58,715 --> 01:02:00,917
Okay, I get it, so stop scaring me.

983
01:02:00,984 --> 01:02:02,786
Alright, you guys work hard too.

984
01:02:02,852 --> 01:02:04,621
Okay, don't work too hard.

985
01:02:04,688 --> 01:02:06,656
-Good luck today.

986
01:02:08,892 --> 01:02:10,327
Did you chicken out?

987
01:02:11,127 --> 01:02:14,464
Hey, doesn't she seem a bit weird now?

988
01:02:14,531 --> 01:02:17,767
How so? She just looks happy.
It's nice that she's cheerful.

989
01:02:17,834 --> 01:02:20,136
No, she's definitely gotten weird.

990
01:02:20,203 --> 01:02:23,139
You're weirder, you punk. You are.

991
01:02:23,206 --> 01:02:24,941
Let's just go catch snails.

992
01:02:25,008 --> 01:02:26,443
Yu-na is really pretty.

993
01:02:26,509 --> 01:02:28,111
Oh, you little rascal.

994
01:02:37,254 --> 01:02:41,224
Wow, it's been a while
since we shoveled together, Hong-gu.

995
01:02:41,291 --> 01:02:43,627
Hong-gu, has your shoveling improved?

996
01:02:43,693 --> 01:02:45,295
My skills are no joke.

997
01:02:45,362 --> 01:02:47,330
I'm more than ready for the army.

998
01:02:47,397 --> 01:02:51,268
It's been a while,
so I'll really put you to the test.

999
01:02:51,334 --> 01:02:53,169
-Got that?
-I'll show you later.

1000
01:02:53,236 --> 01:02:54,904
Brace yourself, you rascal!

1001
01:02:54,971 --> 01:02:56,640
Oh, come on.

1002
01:03:06,750 --> 01:03:10,387
-Go on, give it a try.
-The old man put it like this…

1003
01:03:12,188 --> 01:03:14,124
-You need more strength.
-Yun-hui.

1004
01:03:30,874 --> 01:03:33,310
It's been a long time, Yun-hui.
